WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.772
Today we revise Chapter One.

00:00:01.772 --> 00:00:04.241
Introduction to information processing.

00:00:04.241 --> 00:00:06.393
How data differs from information,

00:00:06.393 --> 00:00:09.241
the five components of an information system,

00:00:09.241 --> 00:00:11.520
and the seven information processes.

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:13.617
An information system, I S,

00:00:13.617 --> 00:00:15.881
uses manual or automated procedures

00:00:15.881 --> 00:00:17.304
to turn raw input data

00:00:17.304 --> 00:00:20.150
into meaningful information, then output it.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.440
There are six main functions:

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.848
planning, forecasting, coordinating,

00:00:24.848 --> 00:00:28.660
controlling, operational activities, and decision making.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:31.346
Data means raw, unorganised facts

00:00:31.346 --> 00:00:33.541
that lack meaning on their own.

00:00:33.541 --> 00:00:35.170
They exist objectively,

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:37.577
without context or background yet.

00:00:37.577 --> 00:00:41.258
Examples: test scores eighty-two, sixty-five, forty;

00:00:41.258 --> 00:00:43.170
or a single barcode number.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:45.592
Five common data types:

00:00:45.592 --> 00:00:49.016
text, number, image, audio, and video.

00:00:49.366 --> 00:00:53.193
Information is processed, computed, and structured data

00:00:53.193 --> 00:00:56.603
that carries specific meaning and aids decisions.

00:00:56.603 --> 00:00:59.804
It has context, relevance, and decision value.

00:00:59.804 --> 00:01:04.606
Examples: class average scores, promotion lists, sales trend reports.

00:01:04.956 --> 00:01:07.180
Remember the core formula mindset:

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:10.188
information equals data plus processing logic.

00:01:10.538 --> 00:01:13.555
An information system has five components:

00:01:13.555 --> 00:01:16.931
purposes, or system functions; data; processes;

00:01:16.931 --> 00:01:18.798
technology; and personnel.

00:01:18.798 --> 00:01:20.450
All five are essential.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:23.314
System functions state the purpose:

00:01:23.314 --> 00:01:27.263
automate procedures, improve a system, or fix problems.

00:01:27.263 --> 00:01:30.998
Example: turning manual checkout into self-checkout.

00:01:30.998 --> 00:01:35.307
Data is the core asset, stored in a database for processing.

00:01:35.307 --> 00:01:39.400
Examples: prices, stock levels, payroll, medical records.

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:43.287
Processes are the procedures, rules, or algorithms

00:01:43.287 --> 00:01:46.541
that use data to achieve the system functions.

00:01:46.541 --> 00:01:51.634
Example: restaurant orders — take order, send to kitchen, print receipt.

00:01:51.634 --> 00:01:57.365
Technology covers hardware, system software, applications, networks, and devices.

00:01:57.365 --> 00:02:01.326
Examples: touchscreens, barcode scanners, cloud servers.

00:02:01.676 --> 00:02:03.701
Personnel fall into two groups:

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:07.033
end users — for example customers and accountants —

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:08.601
and I C T professionals.

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:11.998
Professionals include systems analysts, programmers,

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:16.244
network administrators, database administrators, and technicians.

00:02:16.594 --> 00:02:19.371
There are seven information processes.

00:02:19.371 --> 00:02:21.198
The E D B guide order is:

00:02:21.198 --> 00:02:24.414
collection, organisation, analysis, storage,

00:02:24.414 --> 00:02:27.556
processing, transmission, and presentation.

00:02:27.556 --> 00:02:30.114
Focus on recognising each process —

00:02:30.114 --> 00:02:32.818
not on memorising one fixed sequence.

00:02:33.168 --> 00:02:35.619
First, data collection.

00:02:35.619 --> 00:02:38.389
Second, data organisation.

00:02:38.389 --> 00:02:40.626
Third, data analysis.

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:42.864
Fourth, data storage.

00:02:43.214 --> 00:02:45.063
Fifth, data processing.

00:02:45.063 --> 00:02:47.074
Sixth, data transmission.

00:02:47.074 --> 00:02:49.245
Seventh, data presentation.

00:02:49.245 --> 00:02:54.230
Together, these seven form the full information process chain.

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:56.267
Remember three points.

00:02:56.267 --> 00:03:01.175
Data is raw fact; information equals data plus processing logic.

00:03:01.175 --> 00:03:06.543
Five I S components: purposes, data, processes, technology, personnel.

00:03:06.543 --> 00:03:11.068
Know the seven processes — from collection to presentation.
